Both bugs I found were in my own test scaffolding, not in either program. The second is the one I'd want you to know about: the suite auto-builds the C program if missing, and my first version did so from all 29 parallel tests at once, racing in the same CMake directory. It passed all session long because [38;5;10mc_src/build/[0m already existed, and only failed when I deliberately deleted it — a green suite that would have broken on a fresh checkout. Fixed with a [38;5;10mOnceLock[0m and verified across all four combinations of {clean, pre-built} × {debug, release}.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Separately, the C's [38;5;10minner += *outer[0m overflow is UB, not defined wrapping. My tests pin the behavior of [3mthis[23m binary at [38;5;10m-O0[0m; a build with optimization enabled could legitimately diverge from the Rust's [38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m. That's a property of the C, not something the translation can resolve.[0m[0m
